{"accessible_description":"Three elements of A map through two elements of B into two of the four elements of C. The first and third A-elements share one intermediate and final value; the second follows the other branch.","accessible_description_provenance":"explicit_tranche_diagram_semantic_contract","accessible_name":"Composition of f from A to B and g from B to C","accessible_name_provenance":"explicit_tranche_diagram_semantic_contract","arrowhead_path_count":8,"asset_path":"assets/diagrams/composition.tikz","asset_reference_id":"asset-ref-00028","asset_sha256":"ad4d91333bb7d95c341e168381965ada603782bfbcaa2452096d8f1ddd78be04","caption_tex":"The composition $g \\circ f$ of two functions $f$ and~$g$.","dashed_connector_path_count":3,"diagram_id":"functions-diagram-005","element_node_counts_by_color":{"oldiagcolorB":3,"oldiagcolorC":2,"oldiagcolorD":4},"figure_environment_id":"projected-env-000183","file":"content/sets-functions-relations/functions/composition.tex","formal_object_id":"sfr-fun-formal-0034","formula_ids":["projected-formula-0001172","projected-formula-0001173","projected-formula-0001174"],"instance_id":"inst-00025","line":33,"linearization":["Call the three A-elements the first, second, and third A-elements; call the two B-elements B one and B two; and call the four C-elements C one through C four.","Under f, the first and third A-elements share B one as their middle value; the second A-element maps to B two.","Under g, B one maps to C one and B two maps to C two; C three and C four receive no arrow.","The dashed composite arrows therefore send the first and third A-elements to the same element of C, namely C one, while the second A-element goes to C two."],"linearization_provenance":"explicit_context_reviewed_topology_contract","parse_status":"PASS_TIKZ_PATH_MODEL_CLOSED","path_count":30,"paths":[{"closed_cycle":true,"color_family":"oldiagcolorB","coordinate_count":47,"end_coordinate":[106.8109,75.3598],"path_id":"composition-path-001","path_sha256"